## Artifacts vs SKUs

- Firmware **artifact** = chip + flash + PSRAM + USB class (one PIO env / image).
- Amazon / vendor SKU = catalog row that points at an artifact plus default pin overlays.
- Custom boards are catalog rows (core + flash + PSRAM + USB + pins), not a new `src/` tree.

## P4 combo

P4 + C6/C5/S3 via ESP-Hosted is a later node class. Ethernet-only P4 first. If the desk board is Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6-POE-ETH, the C6 is already onboard.

## Flash and scale

Matrix flash handshake stays Matrix-only (`pio run -e matrix -t upload`, COM3 script). Other boards get their own env and port when that env exists.

Firmware is one node. Size rings from the board profile. Do not hard-code 100k buffers.
